== Problem

+ A delegated agent finds something real outside its scope and writes it in
  its closing report.
+ 🔴 That report reaches one orchestrator once, then is gone. Two stale
  claims about `--set` survived that way through the whole session that
  retired the behaviour they described.
+ `just ask-refactoring` already solves the machine half: a signal becomes a
  filed task with its own template. A finding a person or an agent noticed
  has no equivalent channel, so it competes with prose for attention.
+ Nothing distinguishes a finding that was filed from one that was mentioned,
  so the backlog cannot answer what is outstanding.


== TO-BE

- 🟢 `mt add --template finding` files an out-of-scope observation with its
  evidence, the file it lives in, and what would close it.
- 🟢 Every filed finding carries a `found` tag, so `mt ls 'has_tag("found")'`
  is the whole outstanding list.
- 🟢 The delegation rules say a finding is filed, never reported in prose
  alone, and the agent-facing docs say the same.
- 🟢 A filed finding is `proposed`, so it never competes with the WIP cap.


== Changes

- `.mindtape/templates/finding.typ` — the template, modelled on
  `sweep-size.typ`, with slots for the observation, the evidence quoted from
  what it printed, and the file that would carry the fix.
- `.mindtape/config.toml` — `found` in `[tasks.tags] allowed`.
- `docs/src/contributing.typ` — the rule, in the delegation section: an
  out-of-scope finding is filed before the report is written.
- `CONTRIBUTING.md` — regenerated by `just docs md`, never hand-edited.
- `www/content/agents.typ` — the same instruction for an agent driving `mt`
  from outside this repo.


== Rollback

Delete `.mindtape/templates/finding.typ`, drop the `found` tag from
`[tasks.tags] allowed`, and revert the prose. Tasks already filed stay valid,
because a finding is an ordinary task with one extra tag.


== Out of scope

- Making a gate refuse an unfiled finding. Nothing can see a finding that was
  never written down, so the rule is the enforcement here.
- The sweep's own templates, which already have a channel that works.


== Dogfood

This session produced four findings worth filing and reported them as prose.
The next delegated run files them instead, and `mt ls 'has_tag("found")'`
answers what is outstanding without anyone rereading a transcript.

